Z||000023||Tina||12-28-2001||06:21 PM||||Thanks for the extra pic's. <P>If anybody knows where I can find one cheaper than what JC Whitney sells them for, please LMK<P>Tina <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>BTW <A HREF="http://www.holley.com/HiOctn/ProdLine/Products/ES/ESMP/CarBars.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.holley.com/HiOctn/ProdLine/Products/ES/ESMP/CarBars.html</A> <BR>checked for price on this site...$613  ouch||||reg||1
Z||000024||pherder||12-28-2001||07:43 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tina:<BR><B>If anybody knows where I can find one cheaper than what JC Whitney sells them for, please LMK<P>Tina   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Tina, <P>PAECO sells the Kirk Racing Products roll bars in three flavors!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>A Street bar (2095) (like the Hooker but smaller diameter tubing) for $225.<P>A Slalom Bar (3095)(like the one I put in my 88 Coupe that I sold to Standard) for $375.<P>And a full Roll Cage (4095) for $695.<P>Shipping is:<P>By surface (UPS) $62<BR>By Air           $102<BR>By Next Day Air  $175<P>PAECO Industries, Inc.<BR>2400 Mountain Drive<BR>Birmingham, AL 35226<P>1.800.326.6401<BR>1.205.823.7278<P>Please note that the bar in Standard's 88 Coupe is the OLD style Slalom bar.  The new roll bar and roll cage (meets SCCA specs) has a horizontal bar behind the seats that goes <B>THRU</B> where the ECM is!  I.e. the ECM will/might have to be relocated to fit the bar!<P>I don't know if you can special order the old style Slalom Bar.<P>The bars come "painted" black so they will not rust during shipping.  They will need to be painted or powdercoated.<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
